// Egress seam, registration: a network service announces itself, and what it
// carries, to the orchestrator. Server: orchestrator. Client: network service.
//
// Services dial the orchestrator, as workers do, so a service can sit behind a
// firewall and the orchestrator needs no inventory of them. Each says which
// destinations it carries, and that is how one deployment can have a service
// inside a private network, another on the public internet and a third behind
// a proxy, all served to the same set of orchestrators: the orchestrator gives
// each destination a function may reach to the service that carries it.

